# filename <space> file id on the host
#
# Fill this in and save it as data-release/embeddings.ids. There are two forms
# and the fetch script reads either.
#
# ONE ARCHIVE. Upload syn-embeddings.zip, share it, and give its id here:
#
#     ARCHIVE  1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz
#
# One share setting, one link, and the host's per-file download quota charged
# once instead of twelve times. The cost is that a failed transfer restarts
# from zero. The unpacked files are still checked against the manifest one by
# one -- the archive is a transport, not a source of truth.
#
# TWELVE FILES. Upload them separately and give one id each. A failed run
# resumes by skipping what already verified, and a file that hits the quota
# does not block the other eleven. If both forms are present this one wins.
#
# For a Google Drive link of the form
#     https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz/view?usp=sharing
# the id is the segment between /d/ and /view.
#
# Every file must be shared as "Anyone with the link -- Viewer". Sharing the
# enclosing folder is not enough: the script addresses files by id, so each
# file needs the link permission itself. Setting it on the folder before
# uploading applies it to everything added afterwards.

